ma-exedra" by previous archaeologists. The term might be a starting point for the re-examination of this peculiar liturgical furniture of the churches of Central and Northern Syria.</note></biblStruct><bibl type="formatted" subtype="bibliography" resp="https://www.zotero.org/styles/chicago-note-bibliography-17th-edition">
